[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug, one fix queued. Its own table already shows two causes,
and five of its reports are not a flipped month at all. The parser fix will not close the other
two. Each problem now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Three problems, three fixes. Fixing the parser leaves the other two open.
</Callout>

## The three problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

### `parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first

A day-first tenant books 7 April (`07/04`); the invite says 4 July. Day and month swap, every time,
on every channel except booking-v3's form. This is the bug #4471 describes, and the queued fix is
for this one only.

### `hint`: booking-v3's form tells people to type the month first

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. Day-first tenants on that form (Alder Physio,
Copper Studio, Pale Harbour) type what the hint says, and the form reads it day first. Same flip
for the reporter, different code: the parser fix does not touch it. Fix the hint, or read the
field the way the hint says.

### `day-shift`: the date moves by one day, nothing is flipped

"Tuesday 12 May" on the invite, "Monday 11 May" in the calendar. One meeting on Tuesday in Lisbon
and Monday in Toronto. An invite that arrives before its booking. The desk noted these five as a
one-day move, then filed them under `parser` by tenant. A swap of day and month cannot move a date
by one day; this looks like a time zone conversion at midnight (not confirmed in the code).

## How to tell them apart

- Day and month swapped, booked through booking-v3's form at a day-first tenant: `hint`.
- Day and month swapped, any other way in: `parser`.
- Off by one day, no swap: `day-shift`.

Subject lines do not tell them apart: all three arrive as "Date is wrong". Intake's tag does not
either: it guesses from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant's form.

## What changes for the desk

- [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) stays as it was; this page is where its reports go now.
- Merging on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put all three
  into one ticket. A new decision record should replace 0001, not an edit.

